  "ai_language_tip": "Use polite standard Persian (fa) with formal plural 'شما'; Azerbaijani Turkish, Kurdish and other languages are spoken regionally but Persian works everywhere for business. English is limited to some hotels, travel agencies and private clinics in Tehran, Isfahan and Shiraz.",
  "english_ok": "rarely — Some hotel front desks, tour agencies and private hospitals in big cities; most shops, clinics and drivers speak only Persian.",
  "politeness": "Elaborate courtesy (taarof) is normal: greet with 'سلام' and a polite phrase, use titles ('آقای', 'خانم', 'دکتر'); requests are softened; close with thanks and 'خداحافظ'.",
  "name_tip": "Bookings usually under surname with 'آقای'/'خانم'; many people prefer surname for formal records; Latin spellings of Persian names vary, so spell slowly.",
  "phone_tip": "Mobile 09XX XXX XXXX (11 digits with 0, e.g. 0912 12345678), international +98 9XX; Tehran landline 021 + 8 digits; SMS and messaging apps (WhatsApp, Telegram, local apps) are used for confirmations.",
  "time_tip": "Spoken time often 12-hour with part of day (صبح, ظهر, عصر, شب); confirm am/pm. Dates normally use the solar Hijri calendar (e.g. ۲۵ آبان) — convert carefully; lunar Hijri for religious holidays.",
  "number_tip": "Eastern Persian digits (e.g. ۰ ۱ ۲ ۳ ۴) and Western digits both appear; mobile numbers are read in groups (0912 / 345 / 67 89).",
  "avoid_calling": "Avoid Friday (weekend), early afternoon rest 14:00–16:00 at many small shops, late night, and Nowruz (around 20 March to early April) when businesses close or run thin; Muharram mourning days and Ramadan change hours.",
  "closed_days": "Friday is the weekly day off; many offices also close or work short on Thursday; Nowruz holidays (about 1–4 Farvardin, ~21–24 March) plus 12–13 Farvardin, Tasua/Ashura and other religious days close most businesses.",
  "booking_channels": "Paziresh24, Doctoreto and Snapp Doctor for doctor appointments; Snapp and Tapsi for rides; SnappFood for delivery; Divar for property and services; phone and messaging apps still dominant for restaurants, salons and garages.",
  "voice_menu": "Banks, MCI (Hamrah-e Aval), Irancell, Rightel, utilities and large hospitals use IVR; private clinics often have a receptionist (منشی) answering directly.",
  "callback_habits": "Doctor platforms send SMS appointment codes and reminders; clinics may call the day before; small businesses confirm by SMS or messenger.",
